course: dictionary
lesson: 12921
title: Etna, a name and a volcano
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Etna is a proper noun. It is the name of one special place, so it starts with a capital letter. «Mount Etna» and «Etna» both mean the same volcano, and you can find it in a book about Italy.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Etna is a large, active volcano on the island of Sicily.» Large and volcano tell you it is a big mountain made by fire under the ground. Active tells you it can still erupt, so it is not a sleeping volcano.
explain: «Etna erupted last year, and smoke rose high into the sky.» Erupted is a clue too: a volcano erupts when hot rock, ash and smoke burst out. Even so, «farmers still grow crops on its slopes», because the soil is very rich.
fact: Etna is a large, active volcano on the island of Sicily, in southern Italy.
fact: «Etna» is a proper noun, so it begins with a capital letter, as in «Mount Etna».
fact: Etna is the highest active volcano in Europe outside the Caucasus.
fact: «Active» means that a volcano can erupt, and «erupted» means it burst out with lava, ash and smoke.
fact: Volcanic soil is very rich, so people still farm and live on the slopes of Etna.
exercise: «Mount Etna» is a volcano on which island? | *Sicily | Sardinia | Crete | Corsica
exercise: Why does Etna start with a capital letter? | Because it is the name of a colour | *Because it is the name of one special place | Because it is always the first word of a sentence | Because it is a long word
exercise: «Etna erupted last year.» What does erupted mean? | Grew tall with trees | Went quietly to sleep | *Burst out with lava, ash and smoke | Turned into a lake
test: «Farmers still grow crops on the slopes of Etna because the soil is rich.» What do the words around rich suggest? | *The soil is very good for growing plants | The soil is cold and hard as rock | The soil is too poor for any plants | The soil is made only of sand
test: «Etna is an active volcano.» What does active mean here? | It is a very small hill | It is asleep forever | *It can erupt | It moves across the sea
exam: Which sentence describes Etna best? | A small island with no mountains | *A large, active volcano on the island of Sicily | A long river in northern Spain | A dark cave under the sea
